00-first: reading="When I read books during the year, I forget what I read by December, I can keep track of the books I've read this year and see them all in one place with a short note on what I thought of each one, so I can remember what I read. It works if I can see each book from this year alongside a short note about my thoughts; It must be nothing fancy." focused=null
00-first: reading="New users receive five onboarding emails in the first week, and the unsubscribe rate keeps going up, so new users do not feel spammed while marketing can still use onboarding emails. Do not kill the onboarding emails entirely." focused={"id":"model-c10868c455aaf6a8","text":"What do you want to be able to know, decide, or do about the onboarding emails?"}
00-first: reading="When Socratink learners answer incorrectly, they currently see a red X and may leave, I can leave a wrong answer feeling smarter rather than dumber, so learners understand why their answer was wrong and stay engaged. No gamification; it must work on phones; do not assume an AI tutor chat panel or a whole quiz-engine rebuild is the solution." focused={"id":"model-3b0f6894b051c4ab","text":"What observable change would show that a learner leaves a wrong answer feeling smarter?"}
00-first: reading="In the morning, when I open Tinkery after yesterday's ledger activity, I can know whether yesterday went well and whether the 6am job failed, so I know what to do with the ledger instead of facing a wall of numbers. It works if I can know in like 5 seconds using useful changes per hour and maybe cost; No dashboard; it must not fail silently." focused={"id":"model-7463df1cdf1dcc92","text":"Should detecting a failed 6am job be part of the same morning check, or a separate concern?"}
01-answer: reading="In the morning, when I open Tinkery after yesterday's ledger activity, I can know whether yesterday went well, with a failed 6am job overriding everything, so I know what to do with the ledger instead of facing a wall of numbers. It works if I can know in like 5 seconds using useful changes per hour, with cost only if its way off; No dashboard; a failed job must not be hidden or discovered days later." focused=null
